From 87eaec5a65a3904e237281414cf6bd93bfcb8923 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephan Raj Ignatious Durairaj <signatio@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 9 Jul 2026 19:45:29 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 264/265] traffic separation: avoid full VLAN rebuild on
 redundant/VID-only re-apply

TrafficSeparationTask::reset() always called
TrafficSeparationManager::clear_policies() and rebuilt every trunk/access
port's PortPlumbing instance from scratch, even when nothing changed or
only the private/guest VLAN IDs differed. Recreating already-applied VLAN
subinterfaces detaches them from their bridge and forces an STP
re-convergence (disabled->listening->learning->forwarding), causing ping
loss between agent and controller during traffic separation apply.

This happens in two scenarios:
1. TS_ENABLE fires again with an identical config and trunk port set (one
   event per radio as they each finish configuring).
2. The primary VLAN ID is learned early (e.g. from the backhaul
   association response) while the guest VID still falls back to a
   default; the real guest VID only arrives later once the Traffic
   Separation policy TLV is processed, so the next TS_ENABLE has the same
   trunk set but a different guest_vid.

reset() now classifies each apply against the config/trunks cached from
the last successful apply, before falling through to the existing
clear_policies() + rebuild flow documented in
documentation/images/plantuml/agent/traffic_separation/ts_handle_policies_SD.puml:
  - matches_last_applied(): identical config and trunk set -> skip.
  - only_vids_changed(): same bridges and trunk set, only private_vid/
    guest_vid differ -> TrafficSeparationManager::reapply_config(), which
    updates m_config and re-invokes apply() on all currently managed ports
    without touching the manager's state machine or removing any of them.
    If the retag fails, cached state is left untouched here and only
    updated once the fallback full rebuild below succeeds.
  - otherwise -> full clear_policies() + rebuild, as before.

TrunkPortPlumbing8021q::apply() gains retag_subifaces(), which uses the
new network_utils::set_vlan_interface_id() ("ip link set ... type vlan id
...") to retag an existing VLAN subinterface without detaching it from
its bridge. It is used when bridges/mode are unchanged but the VIDs
differ, instead of clear() + recreate. After retagging, the subinterface
is renamed via the new network_utils::rename_interface() ("ip link set
... name ...") so its name stays in sync with its VID; renaming a live
bridge port does not affect its bridge membership or STP state. A failed
rename is logged as a warning (not fatal, since the VID retag already
succeeded), though it does leave the cached subinterface name out of sync
with the VID it now actually carries until the next successful retag or a
full rebuild. AccessPortPlumbing8021q::apply() is already VID-agnostic and
idempotent, so it is unaffected.

set_vlan_interface_id() checks the "ip link set ... type vlan id ..."
command's exit status and returns false on failure instead of
unconditionally returning true, so a rejected retag (e.g. kernel refusing
the VID change) correctly falls back to clear()+recreate instead of
silently leaving the subinterface on its old VID while the cached config
already reflects the new one.

sTrunkPort gains operator== to support the trunk-set comparison. The
cached last-applied state is invalidated on the disabled/invalid
primary_vlan_id path, on TS_CLEAR, and after a failed apply, so a stale
skip can't mask a real change.

Signed-off-by: Stephan Raj Ignatious Durairaj <signatio@qti.qualcomm.com>
